menu "Gateway: web"

    config GW_MDNS
        bool "mDNS responder and _http._tcp announcement (NET-6)"
        default y
        help
            Answers <network.hostname>.local and announces the web UI. Turned off per device
            with network.mdns = false.

    config GW_WEB_LOGIN_MAX_FAILS
        int "Failed logins in a row before a source address is blocked"
        range 1 100
        default 5

    config GW_WEB_LOGIN_BLOCK_S
        int "First block of a source address (s)"
        range 1 3600
        default 30
        help
            Issue #64: after GW_WEB_LOGIN_MAX_FAILS failed logins in a row an address gets
            429 for this long, without any password check; every further block in a row
            doubles it, up to GW_WEB_LOGIN_BLOCK_MAX_S. A successful login resets it.

    config GW_WEB_LOGIN_BLOCK_MAX_S
        int "Longest block of a source address (s)"
        range 1 86400
        default 900

    config GW_WEB_STALL_S
        int "Longest time a web server may be held by one incoming request (s), 0 = off"
        range 0 300
        default 8
        help
            Issue #110: esp_http_server serves every session from one task and reads a TLS
            handshake and the request headers with blocking receives. A client that sends them
            byte by byte (slowloris) or stops half-way holds the whole web UI and API. If a
            server has been held this long outside the gateway's handlers (and outside the
            drain of a refused authenticated upload), its sessions are shut down.

endmenu
